  /// - `longitude`: Birth longitude in decimal degrees. It sets the local sidereal time behind the rising sign, together with the latitude.
  /// - `timezone`: Timezone as an IANA name such as "Asia/Kolkata", or as decimal hours from UTC such as 5.5. An IANA name is resolved to the offset in force on the birth date, so a summer-time birth is placed correctly. Defaults to 5.5.
  /// - `ayanamsa`: Sidereal frame the chart is cast in. "lahiri" is the traditional Vedic standard used by most software and is the default. "raman" sits about 1.45 degrees below it. "kp-newcomb" and "kp-old" are the two Krishnamurti Paddhati frames. "custom" takes your own value in degrees via ayanamsaValue. The frame rotates the whole zodiac, so a graha within 1.45 degrees of a boundary can change rashi when you switch, which moves both sign factors of the reading.
  /// - `ayanamsaValue`: Custom sidereal frame value in degrees. Required when ayanamsa is "custom" and ignored otherwise. Use it to reconcile exactly against a specific reference program.
