  /// - `doshaClock`: How the six dosha periods are cut. "sunrise-anchored" divides the actual day and the actual night at this place into thirds, which is the division the frame chapter states, and is the default. "clock-hours" is the modern grid of six four-hour blocks from six in the morning; no classical text assigns clock hours, and the grid is only exact at an equinox near the equator. Both sets are returned whichever is chosen, so a caller can show one and reconcile against the other.
